Z||000000||AusFiero||04-12-2001||04:54 AM||||Ok this problem is my fault. I just replaced my gauge faces with white face gauges. Now all my gauges are totally out of wack. Anyone know how to recalibrate these things without or with tearing it all back apart again. I really can't travel to this event with a virtually non functioning speedo and fuel gauge. And tacho for that matter. Ironically my previously troublesome not working well temperature gauge is functioning beautifully now. Help would be greatly appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||04-12-2001||05:18 AM||||Uhhh....I know that someone might have a better idea but if he turns the key to activate the electrical systems (when everything would normally go to 0) can he calibrate it this way? The only thing he would have to do if this works is fill up the gas tank and set it at F for the fuel...<P>I honestly don't know of any other way...<P>Good luck Aus!||||reg||5
Z||000002||Phil||04-12-2001||06:50 AM||||Sometimes the plug-in connectors in the cluster get corroded, just try unplugging and reinserting them a few times. Happened to me once and that fixed it right up. <BR>Good luck <P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
